      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transport from Coimbatore</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Transporting a two-wheeler from Coimbatore to Chennai involves navigating a specific logistical corridor that demands meticulous administrative preparation. While the physical journey is relatively straightforward, the documentary requirements are stringent to ensure legal compliance and seamless custody transfer at both ends.</p>
<p>To avoid customs scrutiny, police checks, or logistical delays, shippers must ensure their documentation is pristine, accurate, and fully compliant with interstate transport regulations. The foundation of this process lies in proving clear ownership and vehicle legality before the bike even reaches the loading dock.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">The most critical document is the <strong>self-attested photocopy of the Registration Certificate (RC)</strong>.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This serves as the primary proof of ownership and identity for the vehicle.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>It is essential that the name on the RC matches the shipper’s identity documents exactly.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Any discrepancy can lead to immediate rejection of the consignment or potential legal complications during transit.</span></li></ul>
<p>Alongside the RC, you must provide a <strong>current Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate</strong>. This document certifies that your vehicle meets environmental emission standards. Although the bike is not being driven on public roads during transit, transport carriers and authorities often verify the PUC to ensure the vehicle was road-legal at the time of dispatch.</p>
<p>Equally vital is the <strong>valid insurance certificate</strong>. Your existing personal insurance policy typically does not cover the vehicle while it is in the custody of a third-party logistics provider. Therefore, you must secure a dedicated transit policy.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">This is where <strong>100% declared-value marine transit insurance</strong> becomes indispensable.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Unlike standard third-party coverage, this specific insurance product provides comprehensive protection against accidental damage, theft, fire, or natural calamities during the entire journey.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>It guarantees that you receive full financial compensation equivalent to the market value of your bike should any mishap occur, offering complete peace of mind for high-value assets.</span></li></ul>
<p>Finally, the <strong>IBA-approved consignment bilty</strong> acts as the legal contract between you and the transporter. This document outlines the terms of service, including liability limits, delivery timelines, and specific handling instructions.</p>
<p>The bilty must be signed by both parties and clearly detail the bike’s condition, including any pre-existing scratches or dents, to prevent future liability disputes. By assembling this core kit—RC copy, PUC, insurance, and bilty—you ensure a smooth, legally sound, and risk-free transport experience from Coimbatore to Chennai.</p>
